WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
Spring, in a small wood.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.590
Birds hop and play.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.750
Twigs bud.

4
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.550
Flowers open.

5
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.460
A man sits among it all and listens: "I
heard a thousand blended notes," But his

6
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.040
head goes down.

7
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.020
Pleasant thoughts, he
says, bring sad ones.

8
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.540
And one thought grieves his heart.

9
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:21.790
What is it?

10
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.770
Everything around him is joyful.

11
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.280
So why is Wordsworth sad?

12
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.720
In this mission, you'll
go back to spring 1798,

13
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.710
when he wrote it, and the book
it was printed in that year,

14
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.430
with no author's name.

15
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.490
You'll see the speaker find
pleasure everywhere he looks:

16
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.550
in birds, in twigs, in flowers.

17
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.800
And you'll track one line about man that
comes back at the very end, changed.

18
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.390
Your mission: explain
why Wordsworth is sad.
